[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Apache Mahout %%VERSION%% is the Samsara Scala DSL and its Spark bindings.
The MapReduce engine and the command line drivers of earlier releases
(kmeans, seqdirectory, spark-itemsimilarity and friends) were removed
upstream, so "mahout <algorithm>" no longer exists.  Run "mahout help" for
the commands that do.

The interactive shell needs a Spark 2.4.x installation built for Scala
2.11:

  export SPARK_HOME=/path/to/spark-2.4.5-bin-hadoop2.7
  mahout spark-shell

devel/spark in the ports tree is Spark 3.x built for Scala 2.12 and is NOT
usable here: Mahout %%VERSION%% was only ever published for Scala 2.11, and
Scala minor releases are not binary compatible.  "mahout spark-shell" tells
you so instead of failing deep inside the shell.  Fetch a Spark 2.4.x
binary distribution separately, or use the jars in %%DATADIR%%/lib on a
Spark 2.4.x cluster of your own.

The jars are equally usable without Spark for in-core linear algebra:

  java -cp "$(mahout classpath)" YourProgram

Mahout %%VERSION%% needs OpenJDK 8; Scala 2.11 does not support JDK 9 or
newer.

%%ETCDIR%%/log4j.properties is the logging configuration shipped by
upstream, for a log4j 1.x setup such as Spark's own conf directory.
Standalone, "mahout classpath" uses slf4j-simple from devel/slf4j.
EOM
}
]
